### Detective Maria Lopez: the Monster path's conscience with a badge.
### Appears once Elliot has killed enough civilians (stat "innocents").

=== lopez
-- start
? q.sq_lopez>=30 -> arrest
? flag.lopez_talked -> again
> A woman in a rumpled coat, at a desk buried under photographs. She doesn't get up. She looks at you like she's been looking at your picture for a week.
LOPEZ: Mr. Alderson. Thanks for coming in. You didn't have to. That's what makes it interesting that you did.
LOPEZ: I've got a board full of dead people who have nothing in common. Different ages, different blocks, different nights. Nobody robbed. Nobody even argued. They just stopped.
LOPEZ: Except for one thing. Every one of them died within a mile of wherever you happened to be that night. Your MetroCard is very chatty.
ELLIOT (V.O.): She's good. She's the first one who's been good. That should frighten me more than it does.
! set lopez_talked ; quest sq_lopez 20
-> choice
-- choice
* "I don't know what you're talking about." -> deny
* [SPEECH 55] "A mile of me is half of Manhattan, detective. You've got a coincidence and a hunch." -> deflect | deny
* [if cash>=2000 & !flag.lopez_bribe_tried] "What would it take for that board to get a lot emptier?" -> bribe
* "It was me." -> confess
-- deny
LOPEZ: Sure. You don't. Nobody does, until they do. You're free to go, Mr. Alderson. I'll be seeing you. I'm very patient, and you, I think, are not.
-> END
-- deflect
LOPEZ: ...Maybe. Maybe you're the unluckiest man in New York. I've met him before; he looked a lot like you.
LOPEZ: Go home. Don't leave the city. If the pattern stops, I'll start believing in luck.
! set lopez_doubt ; quest sq_lopez done
-> END
-- bribe
! set lopez_bribe_tried
LOPEZ: Two thousand dollars. You walked into a homicide squad room and offered me two thousand dollars. For them.
* [SPEECH 45] "For a quiet retirement from one bad case. Nobody's bringing them back either way." -> bribe_ok | bribe_fail
* "Forget I said anything." -> deny
-- bribe_ok
> She looks at the board for a long time. Then she opens a drawer and holds it open without looking at you.
LOPEZ: Put it in the drawer. Then get out of my precinct and never, ever let me see your face near one of my scenes again.
! cash -2000 ; set lopez_paid ; quest sq_lopez done ; stab -5
ELLIOT (V.O.): Two grand. That's what it costs to make a good person stop looking. I'll remember that. I wish I could forget it.
-> END
-- bribe_fail
LOPEZ: You know what, say that again, louder. No? Then here's what happens: I write down that you said it, and I start looking a lot harder.
! set lopez_angry ; wanted 60
-> END
-- confess
LOPEZ: ...Okay. Okay. Hands flat on the desk, Mr. Alderson. Slowly. Tell me the first one.
* Put your hands on the desk. Tell her everything. -> confess_end
* "...Forget it. I'm leaving." -> took_back
-- took_back
LOPEZ: You don't get to take that back. Not in this room. Not with me.
! set lopez_heard_confession ; wanted 120
-> END
-- confess_end
ELLIOT (V.O.): I tell her the first one. Then the next. She writes it all down in a small, neat hand and never once looks away from me. When I stop talking the room is very quiet. It's the quietest my head has been in years.
! set confessed_murders ; quest sq_lopez done ; ending confession
-> END
-- again
LOPEZ: Back again. Either you want to be caught or you want to watch me not catch you. Both are very bad signs.
-> choice
-- arrest
> Lopez is sitting on the stairs of your building with a folder on her knees. Her hand rests near her holster, not on it. Not yet.
LOPEZ: I've got the pattern, the times, the blocks, your MetroCard, and a witness who saw a man in a hoodie leave the last one. It's over, Elliot. Let's do this the quiet way. For both of us.
* "You're right. It's over." -> surrender
* [SPEECH 80] "You've got a hoodie, a train card and a feeling. Walk away, detective." -> talkdown | fight_warn
* "You should've brought backup." -> fight
-- surrender
ELLIOT (V.O.): I hold my wrists out. The cuffs are colder than I expected, and lighter. Everything is lighter.
! set confessed_murders ; quest sq_lopez done ; ending confession
-> END
-- talkdown
LOPEZ: ...A feeling. Yeah. That's what they'll say, too. The DA, the captain, the lawyer E Corp would buy you. A feeling.
LOPEZ: I'm going to walk away. Not because you're right. Because I can't prove you're wrong. Yet.
! set lopez_doubt ; quest sq_lopez done
-> END
-- fight_warn
LOPEZ: Wrong answer.
-> fight
-- fight
! hostile lopez ; wanted 200
-> END

=== lopez_board
-- start
> Photographs, a street map, red pins. A timeline in Lopez's small, neat hand. Your building is circled twice. Under it, a word: PATIENT.
ELLIOT (V.O.): She's drawn my life as a crime scene. The worst part is how accurate the map is.
? flag.lopez_case_gone -> gone
-> END
-- gone
ELLIOT (V.O.): The pins are still here. The file behind them isn't. She'll stare at this board every night and know. Knowing is all she'll ever have.
-> END

=== precinct_sticky
-- start
> A yellow sticky note on the monitor of the corner desk, in block capitals: CASETRACK PW = Yankees1996!  DO NOT REMOVE - SGT. BRODY
ELLIOT (V.O.): The NYPD's cybersecurity strategy, in its entirety.
! set precinct_pw
-> END
